Package: sapfluxr
Title: Comprehensive Sap Flow Analysis from Heat Pulse Velocity Sensors
Version: 0.6.9.2
Authors@R: c(
    person("Grant", "Joyce", email = "neez1977@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre"), comment = "Developer"),
    person("Gavan", "McGrath", role = "ctb",
           comment = "Authored an independent HPV analysis script that informed aspects of the methodology"),
    person("Tim", "Bleby", role = "aut",
           comment = "Scientific review and Excel workflow design")
    )
Description: A comprehensive R package for processing and analysing sap flow data
    from heat pulse velocity (HPV) sensors such as the ICT International SFM1 and
    SFM1x. Provides a transparent, non-destructive pipeline from raw temperature
    measurements to tree-level water use, including multiple HPV calculation
    methods (HRM, MHR, and T-max), selectable pre-pulse baseline options, data
    quality control, baseline (spacing) correction via changepoint and
    dual-stability detection, wound correction, secondary-method calibration,
    sDMA (Selectable Dual Method Approach) for Peclet-based method switching,
    sapwood-area integration, and temporal aggregation. A companion Shiny
    application (shinysapfluxr) offers the same pipeline through an interactive
    interface.
